Army volunteer (Sheen) serving in Vietnam while his Platoon Sergeant and his Squad Leader
(Berenger and Dafoe) argue over the morality in the platoon and of the war itself.

15
01:02:04,137 --> 01:02:10,137
Stone wrote the screenplay based upon his experiences as a U.S.

16
01:06:12,413 --> 01:06:18,413
infantryman in Vietnam, to counter the vision of the war
portrayed in John Wayne's The Green Berets.

17
01:10:20,689 --> 01:10:26,689
Although he wrote scripts for films such as Midnight Express and Scarface, Stone struggled to get the
film developed until Hemdale Film Corporation acquired the project along with Salvador.

18
01:14:28,965 --> 01:14:34,965
Filming took place in the Philippines in February 1986 and lasted 54 days.

19
01:18:37,241 --> 01:18:43,241
Platoon was the first Hollywood film to be written and
directed by a veteran of the Vietnam War.

20
01:22:45,517 --> 01:22:51,517
Platoon was released by Orion Pictures on December 19, 1986.

21
01:26:53,793 --> 01:26:59,793
Upon its release, Platoon received critical acclaim for Stone's directing and screenplay,
cinematography, the battle sequences' realism, and the performances of Sheen, Dafoe, and Berenger.

22
01:31:02,068 --> 01:31:08,068
The film was a box office success upon its release, grossing $137.9 million domestically against
its $6 million budget, becoming the third highest-grossing domestic film of 1986.

23
01:35:10,344 --> 01:35:16,344
The film was nominated for eight Academy Awards at the 59th Academy Awards, and won four:
Best Picture, Best Director for Stone, Best Sound, and Best Film Editing.

24
